{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T12:58:35.551Z","author":"glm-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0147a6b2b1c7f6eaade00ba3","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:58:35.548Z","author":"glm-agent","text":"Design notes: (1) Every RlmLedger SDK mutation now runs through a bounded dead-owner retry: schema field registration, checkpoint save (commitItemMutations), call materialize (create + claim), complete (comments, usage transaction, close, release) and both run-lease acquireLock calls; the SDK's own lock-wait option cannot be used because the item-lock wait comes from workspace settings (locks.wait_ms) while the only per-call lockWaitMs options apply to workspace transaction locks, and raising the process-global PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS would also slow live-owner refusals, violating fails-fast. (2) The retry matches only lock_conflict with reason lock_owner_dead; live-owner and owner-unknown conflicts plus every other error rethrow immediately. (3) The deterministic evaluation item (rlm-eval-<id>, resumable across crashes) also retries its create and description CAS through the same helper. Orchestration parents in adaptive/reconcile/engine are excluded: they are freshly generated ids created in the same live process, so no dead-owner takeover is needed there. (4) Budget default 15s, configurable as RlmLedgerOptions.deadOwnerRetryMs; backoff follows the SDK's published retry_after_ms hint doubled per attempt, capped at 2s, with 50-150% jitter."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T12:58:35.551Z"}],"before_hash":"c91e23e99b5118021cc89d4d7b607f972bb72b882a72cd13326f7f1a8bd00231","after_hash":"d5932c577e96a6dffe0b719e56175656bf88c1c0f8fa6730c47ecee564d83783","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4648b0da885579223305bedcff54d55b6daa90031bf7e4d50d1b0aa9f3411eec"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T12:59:55.381Z","author":"glm-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0147a6b2b1c7f6eaade00ba3","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:55.376Z","author":"glm-agent","text":"Removal note: the package-side bounded dead-owner retry (src/lock-retry.ts, RlmLedgerOptions.deadOwnerRetryMs) and the README storage-section note citing unbraind/pm-cli#1609 can be removed once the upstream pm-cli fix ships and this package's pin is bumped past it; the SIGKILL crash test will keep proving crash safety without the retry. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/36"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T12:59:55.381Z"}],"before_hash":"d5932c577e96a6dffe0b719e56175656bf88c1c0f8fa6730c47ecee564d83783","after_hash":"96c8f9ec73828115987c22bae7a1803057f4254e4c2465b4414a981280f72b0f","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fbd1ed009c3cc1feec558e1a5a9d1977642cd848ec218a6bb5080277a2b786c7"}
